raylibr bundles the following third-party software. Copyright holders are
also listed in the Authors@R field of DESCRIPTION with role "cph".

================================================================================
Bundled source code
================================================================================

raylib 6.0
  License: zlib/libpng
  Copyright (c) 2013-2026 Ramon Santamaria (@raysan5)
  Source: https://github.com/raysan5/raylib
  Included as: inst/raylib-6.0-minimal.tar.gz, extracted and compiled during
    installation. Built from the official 6.0 release by
    data-raw/make_raylib_tarball.R, which removes window backends and
    libraries raylibr does not compile (RGFW, SDL, DRM, Android, Win32,
    memory backends, and the OpenGL 1.1 software renderer). At install time
    tools/patch_raylib.R applies two small fixes to rcore.c (HiDPI scale in
    BeginMode2D() and resetting window flags in CloseWindow()).

raygui 5.0
  License: zlib/libpng
  Copyright (c) 2014-2026 Ramon Santamaria (@raysan5)
  Source: https://github.com/raysan5/raygui
  Included as: inst/raygui.h
  Modified: RAYGUI_LOG wrapped in #ifndef so raylibr can disable its printf
    output (see src/raygui_impl.cpp), GuiLoadStyle() checks the results of
    fread() and fgets(), GuiFontIconBaking() is only compiled when
    RAYGUI_FONT_ICONS_BAKING is defined, and a negative glyph count in a
    style file is treated as zero (also in the allocation sizes), to avoid
    compiler warnings.

